            "setName": "Set 6",
            "question": "Create the tables below and solve the following queries.\nEmployees (EMPLOYEE_ID, FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME, EMAIL, PHONE_NUMBER, HIRE_DATE, JOB_ID, SALARY, COMMISSION_PCT, MANAGER_ID, DEPARTMENT_ID)\nDepartments (DEPARTMENT_ID, DEPARTMENT_NAME, MANAGER_ID, LOCATION_ID)\n1. Create EmpTest from Emp table by copying structure and data.\n2. Add a new row into the EmpTest table for Empno,Ename,Sal columns. In Ename should have the Current User.\n3. Update EmpTest by increasing the Salary of Vaishali by 15%. Confirm your changes.\n4. Increase all the employees salary by 10% in EmpTest table who are working in PUNE\n5. Delete all the Comm data from EmpTest Table.\n6. Delete all the employees in deptno 10 and do not issue a Commit.\n7. Issue a Rollback and reflect changes.",
            "solution": "CREATE TABLE Employees(\nemployee_id NUMBER(6) PRIMARY KEY,\nfirst_name VARCHAR2(20),\nlast_name VARCHAR2(25) NOT NULL,\nemail VARCHAR2(25) NOT NULL,\nphone_number VARCHAR2(20),\nhire_date DATE NOT NULL,\njob_id VARCHAR2(10) NOT NULL,\nsalary NUMBER(8,2),\ncommission_pct NUMBER(2,2),\nmanager_id NUMBER(6),\ndepartment_id NUMBER(4)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE Departments(\ndepartment_id NUMBER(4) PRIMARY KEY,\ndepartment_name VARCHAR2(30) NOT NULL,\nmanager_id NUMBER(6),\nlocation_id NUMBER(4)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO Departments VALUES(10,'IT',101,1);\nINSERT INTO Departments VALUES(20,'HR',102,2);\nINSERT INTO Departments VALUES(30,'Sales',103,3);\n\nINSERT INTO Employees VALUES(101,'Vaishali','Patil','v@gmail.com','9999999999',SYSDATE,'MGR',50000,0.1,201,10);\nINSERT INTO Employees VALUES(102,'Amit','Shah','a@gmail.com','8888888888',SYSDATE,'HR',40000,0.2,202,20);\nINSERT INTO Employees VALUES(103,'Rohit','Kale','r@gmail.com','7777777777',SYSDATE,'SALE',35000,0.1,203,30);\n\nCREATE TABLE EmpTest AS\nSELECT * FROM Employees;\n\nINSERT INTO EmpTest(employee_id,first_name,salary)\nVALUES(104,USER,45000);\n\nUPDATE EmpTest\nSET salary=salary+(salary*0.15)\nWHERE first_name='Vaishali';\n\nSELECT * FROM EmpTest\nWHERE first_name='Vaishali';\n\nUPDATE EmpTest\nSET salary=salary+(salary*0.10)\nWHERE department_id IN(\nSELECT department_id\nFROM Departments\nWHERE department_name='IT'\n);\n\nUPDATE EmpTest\nSET commission_pct=NULL;\n\nDELETE FROM EmpTest\nWHERE department_id=10;\n\nROLLBACK;\n\nSELECT * FROM EmpTest;"
