            "setName": "Set 7",
            "question": "Create the table below and solve the following queries.\nEmployees (EMPLOYEE_ID, FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME, EMAIL, PHONE_NUMBER, HIRE_DATE, JOB_ID, SALARY, COMMISSION_PCT, MANAGER_ID, DEPARTMENT_ID)\n1. Start a transaction and insert a new employee record. Commit the transaction.\n2. Start a transaction, update employee salary, and rollback the transaction.\n3. Start a transaction, create a savepoint named SP1, update salary, and rollback to SP1.\n4. Demonstrate the use of multiple savepoints within a single transaction.\n5. Start a transaction, delete an employee record, and commit the changes.",
            "solution": "CREATE TABLE Employees1(\nemployee_id NUMBER(6) PRIMARY KEY,\nfirst_name VARCHAR2(20),\nlast_name VARCHAR2(25) NOT NULL,\nemail VARCHAR2(25) NOT NULL,\nphone_number VARCHAR2(20),\nhire_date DATE NOT NULL,\njob_id VARCHAR2(10) NOT NULL,\nsalary NUMBER(8,2),\ncommission_pct NUMBER(2,2),\nmanager_id NUMBER(6),\ndepartment_id NUMBER(4)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO Employees1 VALUES(101,'Amit','Patil','a@gmail.com','9999999999',SYSDATE,'MGR',50000,0.1,201,10);\nINSERT INTO Employees1 VALUES(102,'Rohit','Kale','r@gmail.com','8888888888',SYSDATE,'HR',40000,0.2,202,20);\nINSERT INTO Employees1 VALUES(103,'Sneha','Shah','s@gmail.com','7777777777',SYSDATE,'SALE',35000,0.1,203,30);\n\nINSERT INTO Employees1\nVALUES(104,'Karan','Patil','k@gmail.com','6666666666',SYSDATE,'DEV',45000,0.1,204,40);\n\nCOMMIT;\n\nUPDATE Employees1\nSET salary=salary+5000\nWHERE employee_id=101;\n\nROLLBACK;\n\nSAVEPOINT SP1;\n\nUPDATE Employees1\nSET salary=salary+2000\nWHERE employee_id=102;\n\nROLLBACK TO SP1;\n\nSAVEPOINT SP2;\n\nUPDATE Employees1\nSET salary=salary+1000\nWHERE employee_id=101;\n\nSAVEPOINT SP3;\n\nUPDATE Employees1\nSET salary=salary+3000\nWHERE employee_id=103;\n\nROLLBACK TO SP2;\n\nDELETE FROM Employees1\nWHERE employee_id=104;\n\nCOMMIT;\n\nSELECT * FROM Employees1;"
