            "setName": "Set 8",
            "question": "Create the employee table with all constraints.\n1. Find the highest, lowest, sum and average salary of all employees. Label the columns.\n2. write a query to display the number of people with the same job.\n3. Determine the number of managers without listing them. Label the column number of Managers\n4. Find the difference between the highest and lowest salaries. Label the column DIFFERENCE.\n5. Create a report to display the manager number and the salary of the lowest-paid employee for that manager.",
            "solution": "CREATE TABLE Employee2(\nemployee_id NUMBER(6) PRIMARY KEY,\nfirst_name VARCHAR2(20),\nlast_name VARCHAR2(25) NOT NULL,\nemail VARCHAR2(25) NOT NULL,\nphone_number VARCHAR2(20),\nhire_date DATE NOT NULL,\njob_id VARCHAR2(10) NOT NULL,\nsalary NUMBER(8,2),\ncommission_pct NUMBER(2,2),\nmanager_id NUMBER(6),\ndepartment_id NUMBER(4)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO Employee2 VALUES(101,'Amit','Patil','a@gmail.com','9999999999',SYSDATE,'MGR',50000,0.1,201,10);\nINSERT INTO Employee2 VALUES(102,'Rohit','Kale','r@gmail.com','8888888888',SYSDATE,'HR',40000,0.2,202,20);\nINSERT INTO Employee2 VALUES(103,'Sneha','Shah','s@gmail.com','7777777777',SYSDATE,'SALE',35000,0.1,203,30);\nINSERT INTO Employee2 VALUES(104,'Karan','Patil','k@gmail.com','6666666666',SYSDATE,'DEV',45000,0.1,204,40);\nINSERT INTO Employee2 VALUES(105,'Priya','More','p@gmail.com','5555555555',SYSDATE,'HR',55000,0.2,202,20);\n\nSELECT \nMAX(salary) AS Highest_Salary,\nMIN(salary) AS Lowest_Salary,\nSUM(salary) AS Total_Salary,\nAVG(salary) AS Average_Salary\nFROM Employee2;\n\nSELECT \njob_id,\nCOUNT(*) AS Number_Of_People\nFROM Employee2\nGROUP BY job_id;\n\nSELECT \nCOUNT(DISTINCT manager_id) AS Number_Of_Managers\nFROM Employee2;\n\nSELECT \nMAX(salary)-MIN(salary) AS DIFFERENCE\nFROM Employee2;\n\nSELECT \nmanager_id,\nMIN(salary) AS Lowest_Paid_Salary\nFROM Employee2\nGROUP BY manager_id;"
